# Task 2 — Dynamic Property Access

Use the following object:

const student = {
  name: "Rahul",
  age: 20,
  city: "Ahmedabad",
  course: "JavaScript"
};

Create:

const propertyName = "city";

Use propertyName to access the student's city.

Then change propertyName to "course" and access the course dynamically.

Create the function:

getProperty(obj, propertyName)

Examples:

getProperty(student, "name");
getProperty(student, "age");
getProperty(student, "city");
getProperty(student, "course");

The function should work with any object.

Also test what happens when the property does not exist.

